# Exercises Returns & Warranty against the compose stack (`make up`): the demo Customer requests a
# return of a delivered phone, after the requests it refuses, and Staff approve it.
# Run the requests top to bottom in the IntelliJ HTTP client; the token requests store tokens for
# the ones after them.
# It needs a delivered Order of the demo Customer's with a phone: check one out in the Storefront,
# pack its Shipment in the Admin Console, and wait about 30 seconds for the mock carrier to deliver
# it. Then set @orderId to the Order's ID, @variantId to the phone's Variant ID, and @imei to the
# IMEI entered when it was packed (GET /api/fulfillment-shipping/shipments?orderId= shows them).

@returns = http://localhost:8100
@gateway = http://localhost:8000
@keycloak = http://localhost:8180/realms/ecomm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@orderId = <the delivered Order's ID>
@variantId = <the phone's Variant ID>
@imei = <the phone's IMEI>

### The demo Customer's token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=demo@ecomm.local&password=demo

> {% client.global.set("customerToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### Staff token
POST {{keycloak}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=dev-cli&username=staff@ecomm.local&password=staff

> {% client.global.set("staffToken", response.body.access_token); %}

### An IMEI not shipped on that Order: 422 serialNotShipped
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1,
 "serialNumbers": ["490154203237518"], "kind": "RETURN", "reason": "Not what I expected"}

### Two phones when one was delivered: 422 quantityExceeded, with what is available (1)
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 2,
 "serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}", "490154203237518"], "kind": "RETURN", "reason": "Both broken"}

### A return of the phone, naming its IMEI, through the gateway: 201, REQUESTED, with the Return Period
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}"],
 "kind": "RETURN", "reason": "Not what I expected"}

> {% client.global.set("returnId", response.body.id); %}

### The same phone again, as a warranty claim: 422 quantityExceeded, since the return holds the only unit
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "serialNumbers": ["{{imei}}"],
 "kind": "WARRANTY_CLAIM", "reason": "It stopped charging"}

### An Order that isn't the Customer's, or isn't delivered: 404
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Idempotency-Key: {{$random.uuid}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "no-such-order", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "kind": "RETURN",
 "reason": "Not what I expected"}

### Without an Idempotency-Key: 400
POST {{returns}}/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"orderId": "{{orderId}}", "variantId": "{{variantId}}", "quantity": 1, "kind": "RETURN",
 "reason": "Not what I expected"}

### The Customer's own RMAs, oldest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### Staff's RMA approval queue: requested RMAs, oldest first
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas?status=REQUESTED&page=0&size=20
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}

### A rejection without a reason: 400 naming reason
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Staff approve the return, with a note: APPROVED, the decision in its history
POST {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"note": "Send it to the Berlin Warehouse"}

### Deciding it again: 409 rmaAlreadyDecided
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/reject
Authorization: Bearer {{staffToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "Changed our minds"}

### The Customer reads it, with its decision history
GET {{gateway}}/api/returns-warranty/rmas/{{returnId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}

### The Customer can't decide: 403
POST {{returns}}/rmas/{{returnId}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{customerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}
